       * ``<species_name>.flux_direction`` (only used when injecting from a plane, ``-1`` or ``+1``, direction of flux relative to the plane)
 
+      * ``<species_name>.flux_paired`` (only used when injecting from a plane, ``0`` or ``1``, default ``0``)
+        If ``1``, the particles start on the plane itself, at places fixed by the cell and the time step instead of
+        drawn from the random stream. Two species injected with the same plane, flux profile and
+        ``num_particles_per_cell`` then start their particles at the same places. Use this to inject a neutral
+        plasma with an electromagnetic solver: a new particle deposits no current for its appearance, so
+        Gauss's law holds afterwards only if the charge created at each place is zero.
+
       * ``<species_name>.num_particles_per_cell`` (``double``)
 
       * ``<species_name>.flux_tmin`` (``double``, Optional time at which the flux will be turned on. Ignored when negative.)
